<title>USA: C-TEC Corp arranges $410 mln of credit.</title>
<headline>C-TEC Corp arranges $410 mln of credit.</headline>
<dateline>PRINCETON, N.J. 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>C-TEC Corp said Monday it closed four credit agreements totaling $410 million and detailed its plans to split into three companies.</p>
<p>The company said it would use the credit facilities to fund its RCN business and to repay $131 million of higher-priced senior secured notes.</p>
<p>C-TEC also said Monday it filed Form 10 documents with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission detailing its plans to spin off two units, forming three separate publicly traded companies.</p>
</text>
